<section class=\\"vmReportSection \\">
<h2 class=\\"euiTitle euiTitle--medium\\">Methodology and sources</h2>
<hr class=\\"euiHorizontalRule euiHorizontalRule--full euiHorizontalRule--marginSmall\\">
<div class=\\"euiText euiText--small\\">
<p>Findings reported by a Wazuh agent on the host are <strong>confirmed</strong>. Findings matched against the NVD by software version — network devices, hosts without an agent, and services detected by nmap — are <strong>potential</strong>: a version match does not prove the affected feature is in use. Device configuration is checked against DISA STIG and CCSS rules; attack-path likelihood follows NIST IR 7788.</p>
<p>
<strong>OVSS: how findings are scored and ranked</strong>
</p>
<p>Each finding (one CVE on one asset) gets an OVSS score from 0 to 10, never above its CVSS base score:</p>
<ul class=\\"vmFormula\\">
<li>OVSS = CVSS × Context × ThreatMult</li>
<li>Context = 0.5 + 0.5 × (Exposure + Dependency) / 2</li>
<li>ThreatMult = 0.5 + 0.5 × T, where T = 1.0 for a CVE in CISA KEV, else min(EPSS / 0.1, 1.0)</li>
</ul>
<p>The CVSS score is the CVE's CNA score, else an ADP's, else the scanner's (highest CVSS version within each); with none the finding is Unrated. Exposure is 1.0 for the egress router, 0.3 in a VLAN no router connects to another, 0.5 otherwise (and 0.5, flagged, when the asset's VLAN is unknown). Dependency is the larger of the share of other assets that depend on it and its marked importance (FIPS 199: high 1.0, moderate 0.5, low 0.25). An asset's OVSS is its highest finding's; assets are ranked by it.</p>
<p>Tiers: <strong>P0</strong> at 6.75 and above, <strong>P1</strong> at 4.5, <strong>P2</strong> at 2.5, else <strong>P3</strong>. Then, in order: a potential finding not in KEV is capped at P1; a KEV finding on the egress router is P0; any KEV finding is at least P1. An asset with nothing found or looked up is Unassessed, which is not the same as clean.</p>
<p>
<strong>OVSS sources</strong>
</p>
<ul>
<li>
<a class=\\"euiLink euiLink--primary\\" href=\\"https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog<svg xmlns=\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\" width=\\"16\\" height=\\"16\\" viewBox=\\"0 0 16 16\\" class=\\"euiIcon euiIcon--small euiLink__externalIcon\\" focusable=\\"false\\" role=\\"img\\" aria-label=\\"External link\\">
<path d=\\"M13 8.5a.5.5 0 1 1 1 0V12a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3.5a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1H4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v8a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h8a1 1 0 0 0 1-1V8.5Zm-5.12.339a.5.5 0 1 1-.706-.707L13.305 2H10.5a.5.5 0 1 1 0-1H14a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3.5a.5.5 0 1 1-1 0V2.72L7.88 8.838Z\\">
</path>
</svg>
<span class=\\"euiScreenReaderOnly\\">(opens in a new tab or window)</span>
</a>
</li>
<li>
<a class=\\"euiLink euiLink--primary\\" href=\\"https://www.first.org/epss/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">FIRST Exploit Prediction Scoring System (EPSS)<svg xmlns=\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\" width=\\"16\\" height=\\"16\\" viewBox=\\"0 0 16 16\\" class=\\"euiIcon euiIcon--small euiLink__externalIcon\\" focusable=\\"false\\" role=\\"img\\" aria-label=\\"External link\\">
<path d=\\"M13 8.5a.5.5 0 1 1 1 0V12a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3.5a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1H4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v8a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h8a1 1 0 0 0 1-1V8.5Zm-5.12.339a.5.5 0 1 1-.706-.707L13.305 2H10.5a.5.5 0 1 1 0-1H14a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3.5a.5.5 0 1 1-1 0V2.72L7.88 8.838Z\\">
</path>
</svg>
<span class=\\"euiScreenReaderOnly\\">(opens in a new tab or window)</span>
</a>
</li>
<li>
<a class=\\"euiLink euiLink--primary\\" href=\\"https://www.cve.org/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">CVE records (CNA and ADP scores), CVE Program<svg xmlns=\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\" width=\\"16\\" height=\\"16\\" viewBox=\\"0 0 16 16\\" class=\\"euiIcon euiIcon--small euiLink__externalIcon\\" focusable=\\"false\\" role=\\"img\\" aria-label=\\"External link\\">
<path d=\\"M13 8.5a.5.5 0 1 1 1 0V12a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3.5a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1H4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v8a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h8a1 1 0 0 0 1-1V8.5Zm-5.12.339a.5.5 0 1 1-.706-.707L13.305 2H10.5a.5.5 0 1 1 0-1H14a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v3.5a.5.5 0 1 1-1 0V2.72L7.88 8.838Z\\">
</path>
</svg>
<span class=\\"euiScreenReaderOnly\\">(opens in a new tab or window)</span>
</a>
</li>
</ul>
<p>
<strong>Reachability</strong>
</p>
<ul>
<li>Assets in the same VLAN reach each other directly.</li>
<li>Assets in different VLANs reach each other only through a device whose role is router or l3-switch with an up layer-3 interface in both VLANs; the lowest-id qualifying router is used.</li>
<li>Routed VLANs are derived offline from each device's interface names.</li>
<li>Firewall and access-control rules are not read, so a route that crosses a router shows only that the two VLANs are routed, not that traffic is permitted.</li>
</ul>
<p>
<strong>Limitations</strong>
</p>
<ul>
<li>Firewall and access-control rules are not read.</li>
<li>Attacks that need an account (privileges) or a user action are not modelled.</li>
<li>CVSS v4 Attack Requirements cannot be read (no vector string is stored), so a v4 CVE is judged on its other fields; such CVEs are kept, not discarded.</li>
<li>The NIST IR 7788 mapping is coarse (three values), so many routes tie.</li>
<li>The mapping is applied beyond the CVSS version it was written for.</li>
<li>Only the single highest-likelihood route is kept per target and start.</li>
<li>Spare-port lists are truncated by the checklist, so a start may stand for more ports than it lists.</li>
<li>Assets with no known VLAN are left out of reachability.</li>
<li>An unverified asset is shown as unverified, not as safe.</li>
</ul>
<p>
<strong>Sources</strong>
</p>
<ul>
<li>
<a class=\\"euiLink euiLink--primary\\" href=\\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/ir/7788/final\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">NIST IR 7788, Security Risk Analysis of Enterprise Networks Using Probabilistic Attack Graphs<svg xmlns=\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\" width=\\"16\\" height=\\"16\\" viewBox=\\"0 0 16 16\\" class=\\"euiIcon euiIcon--small euiLink__externalIcon\\" focusable=\\"false\\" role=\\"img\\" aria-label=\\"External link\\">
